From cc0780a43b38d7c8b62863779b2eb6635bf5ae87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Oreo.Yang" <2167young@163.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:44:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] validation BUGFIX incremental validation misses

Fall back to full validation of the data when the validation itself
deletes a node (a when that turned false, a replaced default), because
a deleted node can make constraints in other modules or nodes false
that the edit diff never mentioned.

A configuration instance-identifier that requires its instance names its
target in the value, so no schema atoms say which edits can delete it.
Flag such a module in the dependency index and always validate it in
full.

Add tests for when cascades, default replacement, module order and
instance-identifier.
